    "selection_rules": [
      "Existing framework in the repo always wins. Detect via markers BEFORE proposing anything.",
      "Never install a second web framework when one is present, and never a second app framework when one is present.",
      "When the app target is React Native and the team wants device-cloud execution, Detox and Appium are both valid - that is a genuine two-option choice, so ask.",
      "When the app target is Flutter, flutter-integration-test is the default; Maestro is the alternative only when the same suite must also drive a native app.",
      "A repo with BOTH a web app and a native app binds one framework from each list - that is not ambiguity, it is two targets.",
      "Never write automation for a flow whose steps discovery could not locate in the code. Report the gap instead.",
      "Installing a framework is a new dependency: present it at a gate with the exact package, the version verified on the registry today, and the command - never run it unasked.",
      "A stack whose web_automation is null gets web automation only when a JS or TS front end is detected in the repository; bind that front end's framework there - never npm tooling at a non-JS root."
    ]
